ually happened  um  i've always been um attracted to  biopics and i'm always fascinated with  them i i  when they're done well they you know you  it's like a it's  sort of like a history lesson but you  get to really see  the depth of that person's character and  the journey that they went on and this  was  one of those um i think and  it's done so well in the united kingdom  i mean it's it's  it's been extraordinary the um the  amount of people that have  that uh just just got the story and were  gripped from the first episode and have  been  uh it people were just you know bowed  over by it and it is because it's  it's an unbelievable story it how they  finally catch the killer  and the the tiny bits of evidence that  they find  during the years of investigating that  they did or reopening a cold case which  can never be  an enjoyable process because everything  that they are going to look at has  already been looked at in real depth  with a fine tooth comb and they didn't  they didn't catch the killer so the  amount of um  you know gumption that these people had  to reopen it because they had a hunch  that they  there was something there that hadn't  been found  i mean all that stuff just scripts me  and i was also you know when i was a kid  i was  fascinated with with forensic agency  it's coming off a long way  and watching um you know  the youth dna and and forensics  within the story really was uh was  something  really loved how does your approach  change you know as an actor when you're  doing a series like this versus  you know the hobbit or beauty and the  beast like how does your approach change  well you know a role is a role  you don't i don't think about anything  done prior to it and i don't think about  what i'm going to do after this role  it's just about this role you have to i  sort of  clear my mind my head of everything else  and i consume myself  with the world in which this person or  this character exists  um having access to the real person